meta {
  name: Get live
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/health/live
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.status: eq ok
  res.body.name: eq api
  res.headers['x-minerva-request-id']: isDefined
}

docs {
  What the kubelet's liveness probe calls. Answers with the same body as `GET /health`:

  ```json
  { "status": "ok", "name": "api" }
  ```

  The only failure this route is meant to report is one a restart would fix, so it checks
  nothing beyond the process itself — the status code is what the kubelet reads, and a
  non-2xx here gets the container killed and started again.

  A separate path from `/health/ready` even though the two agree today: a probe is bound
  to a path in the deployment manifest, so the split has to exist before readiness has
  something of its own to check, not after.
}
